  "summary": "The npm package context-engine-ai lets AI agents ingest events from any source and query them in natural language, returning ranked, time-decayed results without a vector database, API keys, or configuration. The HTTP server mode exposes REST endpoints including POST /ingest, GET /context?q=..., GET /recent, GET /count, DELETE /events, and GET /health, startable via ctx.serve(3334) or an npx CLI command. Evidence coverage: 161 of 326 packet slices were shown to the model; the rest were withheld by the prompt budget.",
